<template>
    <SiteShell page="features">
        <div class="page-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Features</span>
            <h1>What the engine can prove</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                OpenIDA reports only what it decodes. Every item below is backed by an
                operation the command line can run today. Anything else is named as
                missing, not implied by a menu entry.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Containers</span>
                    <h2>Header decoding</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Detection is by magic bytes, never by file extension.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cols-3">
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <header>
                        <h3>Portable Executable</h3>
                        <span class="chip chip--accent">supported</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>DOS <code>MZ</code> stub and the <code>PE\0\0</code> signature.</li>
                        <li>PE32 and PE32+ optional headers.</li>
                        <li>COFF machine mapped to x86, x64 or arm64.</li>
                        <li>Image base, entry RVA and section count.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <header>
                        <h3>ELF</h3>
                        <span class="chip chip--accent">supported</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>ELF32 and ELF64 little-endian files.</li>
                        <li>Machine, entry point and section count.</li>
                        <li>Section names resolved through the name table.</li>
                        <li>Big-endian files are rejected, not guessed.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card feature-card--quiet">
                    <header>
                        <h3>Mach-O</h3>
                        <span class="chip chip--warn">header only</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>32- and 64-bit magic, both byte orders.</li>
                        <li>CPU type mapped to x86, x64 or arm64.</li>
                        <li>File type and load-command count.</li>
                        <li>Sections and load commands are not decoded.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Layout</span>
                    <h2>Section maps and address translation</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Addresses stay checkable: each result is a number, not an interpretation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col">Field</th>
                            <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
                            <th scope="col">Where it comes from</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">name</td>
                            <td>Section name, trimmed at the first NUL.</td>
                            <td>PE section table or ELF name table</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">virtualAddress</td>
                            <td>RVA for PE, virtual address for ELF.</td>
                            <td>Section header</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">virtualSize</td>
                            <td>Resident size in memory.</td>
                            <td>Section header</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">rawPointer</td>
                            <td>File offset of the section data.</td>
                            <td>Section header</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">rawSize</td>
                            <td>Number of bytes stored on disk.</td>
                            <td>Section header</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">readable / writable / executable</td>
                            <td>Access flags decoded from the flag word.</td>
                            <td>PE characteristics or ELF <code>sh_flags</code></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="section-note">
                <code>open-ida rva</code> maps a PE RVA or an ELF virtual address onto a
                file offset. A value in zero-filled memory or outside every section is
                rejected with <code>binary/range</code>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Reading</span>
                    <h2>Strings, hex and raw bytes</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Three views of the same bytes, each with an explicit bound.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cols-2">
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Printable runs</h3>
                    <p>
                        Strings are printable ASCII runs of at least the requested
                        length, reported with their file offset and byte length. The
                        default minimum is four and the default limit is one hundred.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Canonical dump</h3>
                    <p>
                        The hex dump uses the familiar
                        <code>offset  bytes  |ascii|</code> layout, sixteen bytes per
                        row, with a space after the eighth byte and printable ASCII
                        shown on the right.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Writing</span>
                    <h2>A patch you can audit</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Nothing is written until the whole range fits the file.</p>
            </div>
            <ol class="detail-list">
                <li><b>Validate.</b> The offset and length are checked against the file size first.</li>
                <li><b>Stage.</b> Patched bytes go to a sibling temporary file with the same directory.</li>
                <li><b>Rename.</b> The temporary file replaces the target, so a partial write is never visible.</li>
                <li><b>Report.</b> The result carries the target path, offset, length and the whole-file XXH64 hash before and after.</li>
                <li><b>Keep the source.</b> Pass an output path and the opened file is left untouched.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Surfaces</span>
                    <h2>One engine, three callers</h2>
                </div>
                <p>The CLI, the studio and the agent skill consume the same reports.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cols-3">
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Command line</h3>
                    <p><code>info</code>, <code>sections</code>, <code>strings</code>, <code>hexdump</code>, <code>rva</code>, <code>patch</code> and <code>capabilities</code>, each mapping to one operation.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Studio</h3>
                    <p>The window reads the same handles over its bridge. Without a host it shows a disconnected state and no sample data.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Agent skill</h3>
                    <p>The skill document repeats the implemented routes and the hard rules: no invented sections, no unverified patches.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Contract</span>
                    <h2>Errors that can be compared</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Every failure carries a stable code, so callers never parse prose.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col">Code</th>
                            <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td class="mono">binary/parse</td><td>The container is recognised but its header or table is malformed.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">binary/range</td><td>An offset, length, RVA or patch target is outside the file.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">binary/unsupported</td><td>The operation is not implemented for this container.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">binary/io</td><td>The file could not be read or written.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">handle/invalid</td><td>No live binary has that handle.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">capability/not-implemented</td><td>No engine is connected, or the requested feature is not wired.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Honesty</span>
                    <h2>Not in this build</h2>
                </div>
                <p>These are absent by design, not hidden behind a disabled button with fake output.</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="missing-list">
                <li>Disassembly, instruction decoding and an assembly view.</li>
                <li>Decompilation, pseudo-code and control-flow graphs.</li>
                <li>A debugger, breakpoints or process attachment.</li>
                <li>Import, export, symbol and relocation tables.</li>
                <li>Mach-O sections, segments and load-command bodies.</li>
                <li>Big-endian ELF and any byte order not reported by the header.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="cta-band">
            <div>
                <h2>Check the boundary yourself</h2>
